+**Rendering Formula:**
 The color of a ray $\mathbf{r}$ is computed by alpha blending [S1]:
-$$ C(\mathbf{r}) = \sum_i w_i(p_i) c_i(\mathbf{d}) = \sum_i T_i o_i G_i(p_i) c_i(\mathbf{d}) $$
-where $T_i = \prod_{j<i} (1 - o_j G_j(p_j))$ is the transmittance, $G_i(p_i) = \exp(-\frac{1}{2} p_c^\top p_c)$ is the Gaussian density evaluated in canonical space, and $c_i(\mathbf{d})$ is the primitive color [S1].
