 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Complexity:** Training is 1.5-2x slower and rendering is 25% slower compared to 2DGS due to per-ray texture querying overhead [S1].
-*   **Memory:** Uses a "jagged" tensor structure for textures. Total parameters depend on dynamic texel allocation [S1].
-*   **Performance (DeepBlending):** SSIM 0.907, PSNR 30.03, LPIPS 0.303, 222K points, 21.6M texels, 78.1M params, 70 FPS [S1].
-*   **Performance (Mip-Nerf-360):** SSIM 0.795, PSNR 27.00, LPIPS 0.263, 218K points, 46.6M texels, 152.6M params, 67 FPS [S1].
-*   **Performance (Tanks&Temples):** SSIM 0.835, PSNR 23.43, LPIPS 0.225, 164K points, 10.4M texels, 41.1M params, 121 FPS [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Significantly fewer parameters than GSTex and BBSplat while achieving competitive or superior quality [S1]. Adapts to scene content frequency [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Slower training and rendering than base 2DGS [S1]. Cloning-based densification is incompatible [S1].
+**Time and Memory Complexity:**
+Training is 1.5-2x slower than 2DGS due to per-ray texture querying overhead [S1]. Rendering is 25% slower than 2DGS [S1]. Memory usage is determined by the number of primitives and dynamic texel allocation, with a hard limit of 256 texture resolution per primitive to cap memory [S1].
