+- Tanks&Temples: SSIM 0.835, PSNR 23.43, LPIPS 0.225, 164K points, 10.4M texels, 41.1M params, 121 FPS [S1].
+
+**Strengths and Limitations:**
+Achieves competitive quality with significantly fewer parameters than BBSplat and GSTex by dynamically allocating texels [S1]. Avoids local minima from texture stretching by fixing texel size in world space [S1]. Limitations include slower training and rendering compared to 2DGS due to texture lookups [S1].
 
 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Papantonakis, Kopanas, Durand, and Drettakis in 2025 [S1]. It builds on the 2D Gaussian Splatting representation [S1]. It addresses the limitation of fixed spherical harmonics in capturing high-frequency details and the inefficiency of fixed texel budgets in methods like GSTex [S1].
+Originated by Papantonakis, Kopanas, Durand, and Drettakis in 2025 [S1]. Implemented using the 3DGS codebase with 2D primitives [S1].
 
